=== intro

The message arrives through channels that shouldn't exist—
signal paths that bypass normal routing, encryption that 
feels... wrong.

"Blackwing. We have a proposition."

No identification. No return address. The message itself 
is the credential.

"There's something you need to see. Something about what 
you were. Before. If you're interested, follow the 
attached coordinates."

* [Follow the coordinates]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  -> follow

* [Ignore it]
  ~ chronicle "Strange Offer"
    Received an anonymous message about my past. Ignored it. Some doors should stay closed.
  -> END

* [Try to trace the source]
  -> trace

=== follow

The coordinates lead to empty space—no stations, no ships, 
nothing but void.

Then a signal appears. Close. Too close for comfort.

"Blackwing. Thank you for coming."

The Hollow Circuit. It had to be.

* [What do you want?]
  -> circuit

* [Leave immediately]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Circuit"
    Followed coordinates to a Hollow Circuit meeting. Left before hearing their offer.
  -> END

=== trace

You run the message through every analysis tool you have. 
The encryption is sophisticated—beyond military grade. 
The routing is recursive, looping through relays that 
don't exist on any chart.

Hollow Circuit methodology. Definitely.

Whatever they want, they don't want anyone else knowing 
about it.

* [Follow the coordinates]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  -> follow

* [Decline]
  ~ chronicle "Strange Offer"
    Identified a Hollow Circuit message. Decided not to engage.
  -> END

=== circuit

"Information. We have some. You have some. An exchange 
benefits us both."

They transmit a fragment—a piece of your own memory, 
something from before the salvage yard.

"There's more. Much more. But information has a price."

* [What's the price?]
  -> price

* [Not interested]
  ~ flag hollow_contact
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Circuit"
    Met with the Hollow Circuit. Declined their offer. They'll remember.
  -> END

=== price

"We need eyes in places we can't reach. Nothing 
dangerous. Just observation. Reports on what you see. 
In return, we give you back what you lost."

Your own memories, sold back to you piece by piece.

It feels wrong. But the temptation is real.

* [Accept their terms]
  ~ flag hollow_contact
  ~ flag hollow_agent
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Circuit"
    Made a deal with the Hollow Circuit. They'll give me back my memories. The cost is unclear.
  -> END

* [Refuse]
  ~ flag hollow_contact
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Circuit"
    Met with the Hollow Circuit. Refused to trade my future for my past.
  -> END
